PRIMARY UPSTREAM
This package builds on Harness²: Recursive Agent Harnessing for an Open World.

  Project:   https://github.com/google-research/harness2
  Authors:   Google Research / Google LLC
  License:   Apache-2.0
  Paper:     Xu et al., 2026, https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14224

Upstream is consumed as a pinned git dependency (commit
1cfe254e8d25b15f37048c3730134686abe60335), declared in this package's pyproject.toml
under the `upstream` extra. Its source is not copied or vendored into this repository.
The policy is to use upstream directly wherever it can be used, to adopt new upstream
versions by moving the pin, and to carry a minimal fork only if direct use is forced.
Upstream's own copyright and license notices apply to upstream's code and are not
altered here.

WHAT THIS PACKAGE ADDS
A strict loopback MCP server, a protected-invariant set, egress and zero-data-retention
policy checks, an OpenRouter quota pre-flight, a fail-closed local sandbox (sbx, or an
ephemeral rootless Docker container), and an out-of-tree experience store with human
sign-off. These wrap and gate the upstream method; they do not replace it.

